{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require social media platforms to allow users to opt out of AI-generated content",
        "additional_details": "AI generated images and videos are increasingly common on social media and can be difficult to distinguish from content created by people.\r\n\r\nSome platforms already identify and label AI generated content. We believe users should have the choice to prevent this content from appearing in their recommended feeds.\r\n\r\nThis would not ban AI generated content. It would simply give users greater control over what is recommended to them and allow those who prefer human created content to opt out.",
        "background": "We want the Government to require social media platforms operating in the UK to provide users with a clear setting allowing them to opt out of identified AI-generated images, videos and other content in their recommended feeds.",
